WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.703
Partial updates require deliberate
presence semantics.

2
00:00:03.783 --> 00:00:06.790
In JSON, a property can be omitted or
present with null;

3
00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:08.831
JSON itself has no undefined value,

4
00:00:08.911 --> 00:00:13.617
although undefined can arise in TypeScript
objects or framework code after parsing.

5
00:00:13.697 --> 00:00:16.835
An empty string or empty array is another
distinct value.

6
00:00:16.915 --> 00:00:20.183
Define whether omission means no change,
null means clear,

7
00:00:20.263 --> 00:00:23.466
and empty means a valid replacement or a
validation error.

8
00:00:23.546 --> 00:00:25.703
Do not rely on accidental ORM behavior.

9
00:00:25.783 --> 00:00:27.875
Nested input needs a nested contract.

10
00:00:27.955 --> 00:00:32.465
Allowing a top-level profile property does
not authorize every child beneath it.

11
00:00:32.545 --> 00:00:36.990
Validate and map displayName, locale, or
other permitted children explicitly,

12
00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:39.946
and reject or deliberately discard
internal flags.

13
00:00:40.026 --> 00:00:44.406
Recursive object spreading or deep merging
can reopen mass assignment below an

14
00:00:44.486 --> 00:00:46.643
apparently safe top-level allowlist.

15
00:00:46.723 --> 00:00:51.102
Arrays of child objects need item-level
schemas and authorization rather than

16
00:00:51.182 --> 00:00:53.536
approval based only on the array property.

17
00:00:53.616 --> 00:00:58.387
Dynamic key assignment also introduces
broader JavaScript object-safety concerns,

18
00:00:58.467 --> 00:01:01.736
so avoid arbitrary keys when a fixed
structure is possible.

19
00:01:01.816 --> 00:01:05.934
ORM features such as nested create,
update, connect, disconnect, upsert,

20
00:01:06.014 --> 00:01:10.655
relation assignment, and bulk modification
are powerful persistence primitives.

21
00:01:10.735 --> 00:01:13.088
They are not API authorization contracts.

22
00:01:13.168 --> 00:01:17.025
Do not accept the ORM's nested update
language directly from a client.

23
00:01:17.105 --> 00:01:21.811
Translate the operation's public input
into only the relation changes the caller may

24
00:01:21.891 --> 00:01:25.486
request, and verify authorization for
every referenced object.

25
00:01:25.566 --> 00:01:29.880
Bulk commands need a scoped target set and
all-or-nothing or partial-failure

26
00:01:29.960 --> 00:01:31.856
semantics chosen intentionally.

27
00:01:31.936 --> 00:01:36.250
Generic JSON Patch and JSON Merge Patch
formats also need field-level policy.

28
00:01:36.330 --> 00:01:40.644
Syntactically valid operations and paths
can still address forbidden state.

29
00:01:40.724 --> 00:01:43.339
Authorize every supported path and
operation,

30
00:01:43.419 --> 00:01:48.060
constrain array and nested behavior, and
apply business rules before persistence.

31
00:01:48.140 --> 00:01:50.951
Merge Patch gives null a defined deletion
meaning,

32
00:01:51.031 --> 00:01:54.691
which may not match a domain field's
meaning without translation.

33
00:01:54.771 --> 00:01:57.843
PATCH is an HTTP method and a family of
representations,

34
00:01:57.923 --> 00:02:01.780
not permission to update every property
reachable through the model.
